{
  "comment": "P4.D279 keystone C1 §7 — the outfit-change side effects (v4 lib/wardrobe/outfit-change-effects.ts). Consumed by build-outfit-change-effects-fixture.ts (the main-DB fixture: a user, a default image profile WITH an apiKeyId so the avatar trigger resolves a usable profile, four chats — avatar auto-update ON / a second ON / OFF / an autonomous room with the flag ON — each seating both characters, and a materialized background_jobs table), by cases/outfit-change-effects-tier3.ts (drives the REAL module through this scripted matrix) and by outfit_change_effects_tier3_equivalence.rs (the same matrix through the Rust port). The two character ids are participants only: the module never reads characters, so no vault is provisioned and no mount index is needed. Steps run IN ORDER against one shared turn set; `dropBackgroundJobs` is destructive and everything after it exercises the schedule's catch leg. P4.D282 (the chat-spine half): two `equip` steps drive the chat outfit route's REAL `handleEquipSlot` (v5 `chat_equip`) on the flag-OFF chat — a take-off that reads no pool — so the route's `notifyWardrobeChanged(…, '[Chats v1] outfit-equip')` enqueues the announcement AT ONCE (no turn set) with its DEBUG, and, after the table is dropped, takes the catch leg's WARN while the route still answers 200 (`status` recorded on equip rows). P4.D316 (outfit-history RECORDING, v4 05005c562 + 4ae20977f at e8e17b2d9): every notify / record step carries a `provenance` (default `{ source: 'character', actorCharacterId: <the step's character> }`) and optional `historyIntent`; a `withSet` step also carries the turn's history Map unless `withMap: false` (the 'predates the factory' branch); both come from ONE `newWardrobeTurnContainers()`; `record` passes `repos` FIRST (the pin's signature — the unchanged case garbled it). New ops: `dress` (the REAL chats repository's setEquippedOutfit — no effects), `seedMap` / `clearMap` (the turn Map directly, for the empty-Set-with-a-Map row). Three new chats: `hist` (avatar OFF, both characters LLM) and two operator-provenance chats (`opTyping` — a user seat for characterU selected as activeTypingParticipantId; `opImp` — B's LLM seat impersonated and selected) plus the seat-less `off` chat (the bare operator). A user seat whose characterId is '' is refused by v4's chat schema (UUID), so it is pinned in v5's unit tests only. Every step also dumps `chat_wardrobe_history` (ids / createdAt not dumped) and the turn Map; both sides plant the table on their per-case copy (P4.D315's helpers).",
